_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Fail fast when `styled-jsx` source is missing; don’t silently pass.**

Line 12 currently exits successfully when the source package is absent, which can hide dependency/install problems and defer failure to a less actionable build step. Also, treating “target exists” as unconditional success can leave stale copies after upgrades.



<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-if (!existsSync(source) || existsSync(target)) {
-  process.exit(0);
-}
-
-cpSync(source, target, { recursive: true });
+if (!existsSync(source)) {
+  console.error(
+    "[ensure-styled-jsx] Missing source package at root node_modules/styled-jsx",
+  );
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+
+if (existsSync(target)) {
+  // Consider adding version comparison before exiting to avoid stale copies.
+  process.exit(0);
+}
+
+cpSync(source, target, { recursive: true });
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@searchfn/docs/scripts/ensure-styled-jsx.mjs` around lines 12 - 16, If the
styled-jsx source is missing we should fail fast with a non-zero exit and an
error message instead of silently exiting; similarly, if the target already
exists we should remove the stale target before copying to ensure a fresh copy.
Update the block that checks existsSync(source) and existsSync(target): when
!existsSync(source) call console.error with a clear message and process.exit(1);
when existsSync(target) remove the existing target (e.g. using rmSync or
fs.rmSync with recursive/force) and then proceed to cpSync(source, target, {
recursive: true }) so the copy is always applied from the current source.
```

</details>

